{
  "abstract": "Formalizes the target lowMul3, the three low bits of the product of two 3-bit integers (the product modulo 8), in the unrestricted XOR--AND circuit model of arXiv:2608.30238v1, where XOR and constants are free and either input of a paid AND gate may reuse arbitrary earlier nonlinear wires. Phase 1 proves that the three ANF coordinates agree with integer multiplication modulo 8 on all 64 inputs, and gives an explicit six-gate circuit, one of whose gates reuses two earlier nonlinear wires. Phase 2 adds the derivative lemma (Lemma 8 of the four-gate note in paper/notes/). Phase 3 proves the normal form (Lemma 1), Lemma 2, the pi2 / iota layer with Lemma 8 in the paper's form, Lemma 4 (kernel) and Lemma 6, excludes lambda = 5, and reduces MC(lowMul3) = 6 to four explicit statements. Phase 4 proves the four-linear-gate case (StarFree, Theorem 12 of the note). Phases 5 and 6 prove the three-linear-gate case (lambdaCase_three), so MC(lowMul3) = 6 follows from LambdaCase 1 and LambdaCase 2. The development proves both remaining cases, including TwoClaim and the shared modular feedback lemmas. LowHalfMul3Solution.lean proves the unconditional theorem mc_lowMul3.",
